WEBVTT

00:05.145 --> 00:07.636
Hey, Danny,
did you say good morning to Melissa?

00:08.014 --> 00:09.606
Good morning, Melissa.

00:10.316 --> 00:14.252
- You look lovely today.
- Thank you, Danny.

00:14.420 --> 00:16.411
I think he has a little thing for you.

00:16.589 --> 00:19.319
No, you've got a little thing for her.

00:19.759 --> 00:22.353
I've got a croquet mallet in my pants.

00:23.263 --> 00:25.390
Danny, behave yourself.

00:25.832 --> 00:28.596
Alan, I thought I told you
to keep that doll in your room.

00:28.968 --> 00:31.801
Come on,
he's gotta feed the broad sometime.

00:33.540 --> 00:36.407
- See what I did there?
- You're so clever.

00:36.776 --> 00:38.767
How about spaghetti with pesto
for dinner?

00:38.945 --> 00:41.846
- Oh, boy, with the pine nuts?
- You got it.

00:42.048 --> 00:45.074
I've got your pine nuts right here.

00:45.485 --> 00:46.509
Danny.

00:46.686 --> 00:49.211
Buy one, get one free.

00:50.056 --> 00:53.048
Okay, Alan,
I'm only gonna ask you this once.

00:53.226 --> 00:55.660
Has Little Miss Muppet
moved into my house?

00:55.828 --> 00:57.159
What? No.

00:57.330 --> 01:00.265
Huh, really. Then explain why she's here
when I go to bed...

01:00.433 --> 01:01.957
...and still here when I get up.

01:02.135 --> 01:04.865
To be fair, Charlie,
you have an erratic sleep schedule.

01:05.038 --> 01:07.336
That's not even counting
the drunken blackouts.

01:07.707 --> 01:10.437
You're saying I continually miss it
when she goes home?

01:10.610 --> 01:12.840
Charlie, you missed Easter last year.

01:13.713 --> 01:17.513
Was that the time I woke up
with a Cadbury egg melted in my shorts?

01:19.752 --> 01:21.845
Sadly enough, no.

01:23.723 --> 01:26.385
Okay, just so you understand,
this is my house.

01:26.559 --> 01:28.527
You don't get to invite people
to move in.

01:28.695 --> 01:31.789
Why do you keep harping on that?
She is not living here.

01:31.965 --> 01:35.230
I'm just gonna throw in a load of laundry
before I go to work.

01:36.970 --> 01:39.302
Sure looks like she is.

01:40.640 --> 01:42.835
I don't know what he's talking about.

02:14.907 --> 02:16.238
Hey, listen, I was thinking.

02:16.409 --> 02:18.969
Why don't we bring my bed over
from my mother's house?

02:20.647 --> 02:21.978
We've already got a bed.

02:22.148 --> 02:24.116
This isn't a bed, it's a foldout couch.

02:24.284 --> 02:26.081
You're always complaining about it.

02:26.252 --> 02:30.313
Oh, pfft, I complain about a lot of things.
Like automatic-flush toilets.

02:30.623 --> 02:34.616
Everything's gone before you turn around
and check out how you did.

02:35.228 --> 02:38.527
- What the dickens are you talking about?
- Let's leave the furniture.

02:38.731 --> 02:42.030
- I don't wanna rock the boat.
- How is getting a bed rocking the boat?

02:42.235 --> 02:43.532
This is our room, isn't it?

02:43.736 --> 02:48.332
Well, yeah. And no.
I mean, it's still Charlie's house.

02:48.675 --> 02:50.575
- But you pay rent?
- Of course.

02:50.743 --> 02:53.143
The number fluctuates
depending on the economy...

02:53.313 --> 02:56.976
...and whether Charlie is conscious
on the first of the month. But I pay.

02:57.150 --> 02:59.948
Okay, then you need to start
standing up to him.

03:00.119 --> 03:02.053
Oh, please. I stand up to him plenty.

03:02.255 --> 03:03.313
Is that so?

03:07.493 --> 03:10.485
You think he likes unsalted butter?
He does not.

03:11.998 --> 03:13.966
Now, you listen to me, Alan Harper.

03:14.133 --> 03:16.658
You are a strong, assertive man.

03:16.836 --> 03:18.997
I know that
because I couldn't be with you...

03:19.172 --> 03:20.696
...if you were anything less.

03:21.341 --> 03:22.672
Oh, well, yeah, I am.

03:22.842 --> 03:27.040
You know, I don't wanna flaunt
my strong assertiveness...

03:27.213 --> 03:30.671
...by, you know, asking for stuff.

03:31.050 --> 03:33.211
Tell your brother
we're moving my bed here...

03:33.386 --> 03:37.083
...and if he doesn't like it,
well, then that is just his tough noogies.

03:38.157 --> 03:40.022
- Okay, I will tell him.
- Good.

03:40.193 --> 03:41.455
But slowly.

03:42.161 --> 03:43.685
In increments.

03:43.863 --> 03:45.091
As I did with the butter.

03:46.199 --> 03:50.602
- And how long did that take?
- That is not important.

03:51.237 --> 03:55.196
What's important is this is now
a low-sodium, heart-smart household.

03:56.109 --> 03:59.909
He thinks he's fooling me, but he's not.
She's living here.

04:00.079 --> 04:02.707
He moved her in right under my nose.

04:02.882 --> 04:04.042
So?

04:04.884 --> 04:10.481
So? This is the unsalted butter again,
but, you know, writ large.

04:11.858 --> 04:14.349
What difference does it make
if she lives here?

04:14.527 --> 04:16.893
What difference? Are you kidding?

04:17.063 --> 04:18.462
First it's him and his kid...

04:18.631 --> 04:21.930
...and now he's shacking up
with Strawberry Shortcake.

04:22.468 --> 04:25.198
- He pays rent, doesn't he?
- I don't know.

04:25.371 --> 04:26.565
Once, maybe.

04:28.074 --> 04:29.473
He says he did.

04:29.909 --> 04:32.742
So why do you care
who he has in his room?

04:32.912 --> 04:36.780
I care
because there's a principle involved.

04:36.949 --> 04:39.816
- A principle?
- Yes, I made a rule.

04:39.986 --> 04:42.648
Ohh. You made a rule.

04:43.823 --> 04:45.313
Yes, I made a rule.

04:45.491 --> 04:48.756
And I'm making another one:
You do not get to mock my rules.

04:49.162 --> 04:50.322
You're being silly.

04:50.496 --> 04:52.987
Melissa is a wonderful girl,
they love each other...

04:53.166 --> 04:54.497
...and she makes him happy.

04:54.667 --> 04:57.227
And I care about that because?

04:58.070 --> 05:00.334
Because the Charlie
that I fell in love with...

05:00.506 --> 05:02.770
...cares about
other people's happiness.

05:02.942 --> 05:05.433
- That's the Charlie you fell in love with?
- Yes.

05:05.611 --> 05:07.806
Well, joke's on you.

05:08.881 --> 05:13.750
That whole nice-guy thing was a big act
to get you to have sex with me. Ha, ha.

05:14.987 --> 05:17.512
I know you'll do the right thing,
Charlie.

05:17.690 --> 05:19.487
Oh, you do, huh?

05:21.427 --> 05:24.692
Most of the time,
I'm not even sure what the right thing is.

05:29.335 --> 05:31.132
- Hey.
- Hey.

05:31.304 --> 05:32.828
- Got a minute?
- I'm reading.

05:33.005 --> 05:34.905
Okay, we'll talk later.

05:38.077 --> 05:39.840
- He's busy.
Damn it, Alan, get back out there!

05:40.012 --> 05:43.140
But I gotta pee.
- You already peed. Now go.

05:44.217 --> 05:46.208
Go, get back out there.

05:48.488 --> 05:50.149
Hey-ho.

05:50.857 --> 05:52.620
What do you want, Alan?

05:52.792 --> 05:56.751
Well, as you know,
I pay my fair share of rent around here.

05:56.929 --> 06:00.330
We probably have
different definitions of fair.

06:00.500 --> 06:04.698
And share. And rent. But go on.

06:05.071 --> 06:09.269
I just don't think I need your permission
when it comes to Melissa living with me.

06:09.442 --> 06:11.672
Well, you're wrong.
Nice talking to you.

06:12.178 --> 06:15.011
- Charlie. I would hope that...
- Don't "Charlie" me.

06:15.181 --> 06:17.911
This is my house. Not yours, mine.

06:18.084 --> 06:19.745
The fact is, if Melissa moves in...

06:19.952 --> 06:23.046
...that means you've got more people
living here than I do.

06:23.222 --> 06:26.385
- So?
- So there's a principle involved.

06:30.963 --> 06:33.193
That we must discuss.

06:34.200 --> 06:35.724
Okay, so, what's the principle?

06:41.274 --> 06:43.674
The principle is that...

06:45.111 --> 06:47.579
...you're my brother
and I want you to be happy.

06:49.549 --> 06:53.144
So Melissa can stay? I mean, move in?

06:56.856 --> 06:58.380
Sure.

07:01.394 --> 07:02.486
Well, all right, then.

07:08.334 --> 07:09.631
Oh!

07:17.510 --> 07:18.704
You know, I was thinking.

07:18.878 --> 07:23.042
You've got me, Alan's got Melissa,
even Jake's got a girlfriend.

07:23.215 --> 07:26.275
We need to find somebody
for Sir Lancelot.

07:27.320 --> 07:29.083
Your cat?

07:29.789 --> 07:32.587
Yeah.
Doesn't he deserve some happiness?

07:32.758 --> 07:35.727
He can lick his own crotch.
What else does he need?

07:37.096 --> 07:40.896
Come on, Charlie, why shouldn't he have
some companionship?

07:41.067 --> 07:44.434
All right. How about we get him
a nice lady coyote?

07:45.938 --> 07:48.736
- Charlie.
- What? Lt'd be good for old Lance.

07:48.908 --> 07:53.845
- Get a little exercise running for his life.
- You're terrible.

07:56.315 --> 07:57.805
Let the machine get it.

07:57.984 --> 07:59.042
&lt;i>Hi, this is Alan.&lt;/i>

07:59.218 --> 08:02.654
&lt;i>And this is Melissa. We're not home
and neither are Charlie and Chelsea.&lt;/i>

08:02.822 --> 08:06.553
&lt;i>Charlie might be home,
but he's probably in no condition to answer.&lt;/i>

08:10.196 --> 08:12.130
&lt;i>Leave a message
when you hear the beep.&lt;/i>

08:12.298 --> 08:14.357
&lt;i>- Beep!
- Beep!&lt;/i>

08:16.369 --> 08:18.894
&lt;i>Hello, Charlie? It's your mother.&lt;/i>

08:19.071 --> 08:21.596
&lt;i>Remember me? The woman
who carried you in her womb...&lt;/i>

08:21.774 --> 08:24.607
&lt;i>... for roughly seven and a half months?&lt;/i>

08:24.777 --> 08:26.938
&lt;i>Anyway, I'd say call me,
but what's the point?&lt;/i>

08:27.113 --> 08:29.775
&lt;i>I've long since given up expecting
any kind of consideration or...&lt;/i>

08:31.951 --> 08:33.384
Seven and a half months?

08:33.886 --> 08:36.354
She said,
"If God wanted us to lose our figures...

08:36.522 --> 08:39.719
...he wouldn't have invented C-sections
and incubators."

08:40.426 --> 08:42.394
- Hey, all.
- We're home.

08:42.561 --> 08:45.325
- Oh, boy.
Hi.

08:45.998 --> 08:48.865
- Charlie.
- Hi.

08:49.368 --> 08:52.804
Just so you know, Melissa and I
are gonna put our food on the bottom...

08:52.972 --> 08:55.167
...you take the top
and we'll split the door.

08:55.341 --> 08:58.333
- That's a great idea.
- No, it's not. It's my refrigerator.

08:58.511 --> 08:59.739
Be quiet.

08:59.912 --> 09:01.675
- I bought it. I paid for it.
- Charlie.

09:01.847 --> 09:04.873
- The whole thing, not just half.
- Stop being a child.

09:05.051 --> 09:09.044
I'm not gonna forfeit a grape soda
just because I put it on the wrong shelf.

09:10.823 --> 09:12.791
- Mind if we join you guys?
- Sure.

09:12.958 --> 09:16.018
&lt;i>- What are we watching?
- An Odd Couple rerun.&lt;/i>

09:16.195 --> 09:18.390
I never really liked that show.

09:18.564 --> 09:20.589
- Why not?
- Well, I didn't buy the premise.

09:20.766 --> 09:22.563
Who would put up with somebody...

09:22.735 --> 09:25.568
...who drives them crazy
for all those years?

09:32.344 --> 09:35.074
I mean, it would be different
if they were related.

09:40.252 --> 09:42.413
That was fun
picking out our wedding crystal.

09:42.588 --> 09:44.886
Oh, yeah. Barrel of Monkeys.

09:45.224 --> 09:47.158
I'm so excited
about that big punchbowl.

09:47.326 --> 09:49.191
You know
what would be really exciting?

09:49.361 --> 09:53.730
Next time you ask me to go shopping
with you, use it to cave in my skull.

09:58.804 --> 10:00.396
What the hell is this?

10:01.040 --> 10:02.132
Look who's here.

10:02.308 --> 10:05.175
Hey, dude. Party down.

10:07.179 --> 10:08.203
What are you doing?

10:08.380 --> 10:09.677
We invited a few friends over.

10:09.849 --> 10:11.316
You don't have any friends.

10:11.484 --> 10:14.817
Yeah, but Melissa does,
so now they're mine too.

10:14.987 --> 10:16.818
They don't really like you.

10:16.989 --> 10:18.115
They do too.

10:18.290 --> 10:20.952
Dream on, meat puppet.

10:21.660 --> 10:23.287
Who said you could have a party?

10:23.462 --> 10:25.054
I'm sorry. I thought we lived here.

10:25.231 --> 10:27.358
Must we check with you
about everything we do?

10:27.533 --> 10:29.091
Yes.

10:30.136 --> 10:33.663
What's that guy drinking?
Is that my grape soda?

10:34.140 --> 10:35.732
It was on our shelf.

10:35.908 --> 10:37.705
What did I tell you?

10:38.611 --> 10:39.635
Okay, that's it.

10:39.812 --> 10:42.110
- Charlie.
- No, no, no... This is not acceptable.

10:42.815 --> 10:44.749
Hey, everybody.

10:45.417 --> 10:47.146
Everybody listen up.

10:49.088 --> 10:52.990
Party's over.
Pack up your crap and get out.

10:57.630 --> 10:58.892
I'm not kidding.

11:00.232 --> 11:02.097
One.

11:03.803 --> 11:05.464
I'm counting to three by the way.

11:07.673 --> 11:08.799
Two.

11:11.977 --> 11:14.138
- Ah, screw it, I'll leave.
Charlie.

11:14.313 --> 11:15.746
Forget it. I'm out of here.

11:19.385 --> 11:21.649
See what happens
when I do the right thing?

11:29.895 --> 11:32.386
Okay,
I think you're really overreacting...

11:32.565 --> 11:35.534
...but if you wanna spend the night
at a hotel, fine.

11:36.068 --> 11:39.401
No, I will not come over there
for a quickie.

11:39.939 --> 11:41.964
Goodbye, Charlie.

11:42.675 --> 11:44.165
He just needs to cool off.

11:44.343 --> 11:45.742
We're really sorry, Chelsea.

11:45.911 --> 11:49.005
We should've talked to you guys
before inviting our friends over.

11:49.181 --> 11:50.671
Your friends.

11:53.686 --> 11:57.178
We need some system where we give
each other a heads up about guests.

11:57.356 --> 11:58.516
That's a great idea.

11:58.891 --> 12:02.520
Excuse me, since when do you two
call the shots around here?

12:03.262 --> 12:05.162
What are you talking about?

12:07.032 --> 12:09.000
All right, ladies.

12:10.035 --> 12:11.730
Let's make something very clear.

12:13.372 --> 12:15.272
There's an established pecking order...

12:15.441 --> 12:19.002
...that needs to be honored.
- Oh, really? And what might that be?

12:19.979 --> 12:23.176
Wow. Heh, heh. Do I have to spell it out?

12:23.682 --> 12:24.740
Please do.

12:25.718 --> 12:26.776
Fine.

12:26.952 --> 12:30.547
When Charlie is not here,
I am in charge.

12:38.964 --> 12:40.989
That's okay, isn't it?

12:50.442 --> 12:52.672
- Yeah?
Room service.

13:02.121 --> 13:04.521
Guess who got himself
kicked out of the house?

13:05.891 --> 13:08.985
Ow! Ow! Cut it out!

13:11.764 --> 13:12.890
What are you doing here?

13:13.065 --> 13:14.862
I didn't have any place else to go.

13:15.034 --> 13:17.127
Well, I got news for you.
You still don't.

13:17.303 --> 13:18.736
Come on, Charlie.

13:18.904 --> 13:21.566
Alan, you're the reason
I'm here in the first place.

13:21.740 --> 13:23.765
I know,
I might've crossed a bit of a line.

13:23.943 --> 13:25.467
A bit of a line?

13:26.912 --> 13:28.777
You moved your girlfriend
into my house.

13:28.981 --> 13:31.279
You invited strangers over
without my permission.

13:31.483 --> 13:33.280
And then to add insult to injury...

13:33.485 --> 13:36.215
...you show up here
with your ugly frigging dummy?

13:37.423 --> 13:40.483
Did you hear that? He called you ugly.

13:43.062 --> 13:44.086
Goodbye, Alan.

13:44.263 --> 13:45.787
Wait, wait, wait.

13:45.998 --> 13:48.990
L... I brought you a peace offering.

13:49.401 --> 13:52.097
- That's my 10-year-old Scotch.
- No, it's not.

13:52.271 --> 13:53.329
Yes, it is.

13:55.941 --> 13:57.101
I saw him take it.

13:57.876 --> 13:59.810
Damn it, Danny,
what is wrong with you?

13:59.979 --> 14:01.071
What's wrong with me?

14:01.246 --> 14:04.647
You're the one with your hand
between my little wooden cheeks.

14:05.451 --> 14:07.442
All right, all right, enough. Enough.

14:08.587 --> 14:10.748
If I'm gonna drink Scotch,
I'm gonna need ice.

14:10.923 --> 14:14.154
- There's a machine down the hall.
- Be right back.

14:21.567 --> 14:24.536
Yeah, like I don't have ice.

14:33.445 --> 14:35.640
Thanks for letting me back in.

14:36.315 --> 14:38.943
You were crying in the hallway.

14:41.320 --> 14:43.811
The other guests complained.

14:44.623 --> 14:46.386
Still, it's very considerate of you.

14:46.825 --> 14:49.191
Shut up and drink my Scotch.

14:50.596 --> 14:51.961
Cheers.

14:52.498 --> 14:54.090
Bite me.

14:58.070 --> 14:59.367
This is kind of fun though.

14:59.571 --> 15:02.438
You and me sharing a hotel room
just like when we were kids.

15:02.608 --> 15:04.337
Swell.

15:04.843 --> 15:07.505
Remember that time Mom took us
on that Caribbean cruise?

15:07.680 --> 15:10.581
- We had our own cabin?
- Yeah.

15:10.749 --> 15:13.513
Took us three days to figure out
Mom was on another boat.

15:16.789 --> 15:18.416
- Good times.
- Mm.

15:21.860 --> 15:24.021
We've lost our house, Charlie.

15:28.600 --> 15:30.568
Your house. We've lost your house.

15:31.737 --> 15:33.034
I know.

15:33.205 --> 15:36.504
- How did this happen?
- Slowly.

15:37.342 --> 15:39.333
In increments.

15:39.511 --> 15:41.945
Starting with the butter.

15:43.182 --> 15:44.376
I can see that now.

15:44.550 --> 15:47.144
The problem is, the women
have established a beachhead.

15:49.421 --> 15:51.389
- What?
- Nothing, nothing.

15:51.557 --> 15:54.856
You just reminded me
why I bought a house in Malibu.

15:56.929 --> 16:00.456
The thing is, if we go back,
we'll appear weak.

16:00.632 --> 16:02.122
I don't mind that.

16:03.202 --> 16:04.567
No, no, no. We need a plan.

16:04.737 --> 16:08.070
We need to figure out some way
to drive a wedge between those two.

16:08.240 --> 16:10.765
- You know, divide and conquer.
- Yeah, but how?

16:11.910 --> 16:14.879
I'm not sure.
Maybe we should sleep on it.

16:16.715 --> 16:18.273
Wanna watch some porn first?

16:21.286 --> 16:22.446
No.

16:24.356 --> 16:25.414
Why not?

16:27.726 --> 16:30.957
I'm drunk in bed
in a hotel room with my brother...

16:31.163 --> 16:34.155
...and you wanna know
why I don't wanna watch porn?

16:36.201 --> 16:40.228
Okay. Okay, I get it.
You don't wanna watch porn.

16:50.482 --> 16:52.450
Mind if I watch?

17:01.627 --> 17:04.152
- So they both just up and left, huh?
- Yeah.

17:04.329 --> 17:08.095
- Those boneless chickens.
- They'll be back.

17:08.267 --> 17:10.758
They just have to get used
to the way things are now.

17:10.936 --> 17:13.336
- Damn right.
- Girl power, my bitches.

17:15.307 --> 17:18.640
Hey, Berta, why don't you whip us up
some French toast to celebrate.

17:23.916 --> 17:26.316
Or we could do it.

17:27.119 --> 17:30.054
Good plan, my bitches.

17:32.024 --> 17:35.187
Hello, anybody home?
- In here.

17:35.360 --> 17:37.794
Oh, what a nice surprise.

17:37.963 --> 17:41.626
Good morning, ladies. Berta.

17:41.800 --> 17:43.665
Botox.

17:45.003 --> 17:47.130
So where are the boys this morning?

17:47.306 --> 17:50.673
Oh, well,
Charlie's off sulking in a hotel.

17:50.843 --> 17:53.573
Oh, really? Well, what about Alan?

17:53.745 --> 17:56.305
Oh, Alan's too cheap for a hotel.

17:56.481 --> 17:58.676
I see. And what brought this on?

17:58.851 --> 18:00.478
A lot of macho nonsense.

18:00.652 --> 18:05.521
- Mmm. And Alan?
- Just nonsense.

18:05.691 --> 18:07.886
No kidding. Well, I'm glad to see...

18:08.060 --> 18:10.688
...you didn't let them get away with it.
Thank you.

18:10.863 --> 18:13.491
And I'm doubly pleased
that you two have managed...

18:13.665 --> 18:16.327
...to put aside
your somewhat distasteful history...

18:16.501 --> 18:18.935
...and bond the way
you obviously have.

18:19.104 --> 18:20.435
What distasteful history?

18:20.606 --> 18:23.700
Oh, come on,
let them make my breakfast first.

18:24.643 --> 18:27.510
- What are you talking about?
- A lot of women might resent...

18:27.679 --> 18:31.240
...the former lover of their fiancé
living in the same house as them.

18:32.718 --> 18:35.118
It ain't me, start cooking.

18:36.722 --> 18:39.088
- You and Charlie?
- Just one little weekend.

18:39.291 --> 18:42.692
If I knew what kind of man he was,
I never would've let him touch me.

18:42.861 --> 18:45.056
- What's that mean?
- Oh, he's fine for you.

18:45.230 --> 18:46.424
Fine for me?

18:46.598 --> 18:48.225
Well, I've got an early meeting.

18:48.901 --> 18:51.267
Nice to see you, girls.

18:51.436 --> 18:54.405
Why didn't you tell me?
I thought you were my friend.

18:57.042 --> 19:00.102
If it weren't for me,
your ass would've been gone a long...

19:00.746 --> 19:03.306
I believe the balance of power
is restored.

19:04.182 --> 19:06.150
- Thanks, Mom.
- Thank you.

19:08.921 --> 19:10.889
You owe me large.

19:19.364 --> 19:21.525
Sweetheart,
I think you're overreacting...

19:21.700 --> 19:24.669
...but if you wanna spend the night
in a hotel, that's fine.

19:24.836 --> 19:27.327
Hey, you want me to come over
for a quickie?

19:27.506 --> 19:28.530
Kidding.

19:28.707 --> 19:31.175
Love you. Damn.

19:31.343 --> 19:33.277
Hey, at least Chelsea's coming back.

19:33.445 --> 19:36.073
Melissa said she'll never set foot
in this house again.

19:36.248 --> 19:38.341
All's well that ends well, huh?

19:39.918 --> 19:41.715
Bite me.

19:46.391 --> 19:49.451
Oh, come on, the important thing is
we got the house back...

19:49.628 --> 19:51.755
...and we're once again
kings of the castle.

19:51.930 --> 19:53.261
That's true.

19:53.432 --> 19:55.696
Celeste and I are gonna be
studying in my room.

19:55.867 --> 19:57.232
Okay.

19:57.769 --> 20:01.000
Oh, right. Set another place for dinner.
She's gonna be joining us.

20:01.573 --> 20:03.473
Fine.

20:03.642 --> 20:07.476
- Also, she's a vegetarian, so no meat.
- Got it.

20:07.646 --> 20:10.274
- Come on, Jake.
- Coming.

20:14.052 --> 20:15.815
Kings of the castle, my ass.

20:16.355 --> 20:18.687
We're whipped
unto the third generation.
